english_question:
The figure is a planar unfolding of a geometric body, where ABCD is a square, and E and F are the midpoints of PA and PD, respectively. In this geometric body, the following four conclusions are given: 
① Line BE and line CF are skew; 
② Line BE and line AF are skew; 
③ Line EF is parallel to plane PBC; 
④ Plane BCE is perpendicular to plane PAD. 
How many of the statements are correct?

In the figure, which of the following reasoning statements is correct? ( )
Because ∠A + ∠D = 180°, therefore AD ∥ BC;
Because ∠C + ∠D = 180°, therefore AB ∥ CD;
Because ∠A + ∠D = 180°, therefore AB ∥ CD;
Because ∠A + ∠C = 180°, therefore AB ∥ CD

A square ABCD with a side length of 1 is folded along the diagonal BD to form a triangular prism C-ABD. The front view and top view are shown in the figure. What is the area of the left view? ( ) 
A. \textstyle{\frac{1}{4}}
B. \textstyle{\frac{1}{2}}
C. \textstyle{\frac{1}{6}}
D. \frac{1}{8}

The three views of a certain geometric body are shown in the figure. What is the volume of this geometric body? ( )
A. 6 + \frac{\pi}{8}
B. 6 + \frac{\pi}{6}
C. 4 + \frac{\pi}{8}
D. 4 + \frac{\pi}{6}
